From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover the bundled cxxopts and zlib-ng
 licences

The extension statically compiles in the `src/external/zlib-ng`
sources (zlib licence) and, through `tools/rapidgzip.cpp` and
`tools/ibzip2.cpp` (the bundled CLI entry points), the
`src/external/cxxopts` header (MIT, Jarryd Beck). The explicit
`license-files` list only names this package's own two licences, so
it does not fall back to setuptools' `LICEN[CS]E*` auto-discovery
glob and neither dependency's licence ships in the wheel. Confirmed on
the real published PyPI wheel (rapidgzip-0.16.1-cp312-*-x86_64):
dist-info carries only LICENSE-APACHE and LICENSE-MIT.

`python/rapidgzip/src` is a symlink to `librapidarchive/src`, and
`MANIFEST.in` already ships both files in the sdist, so the added
entries resolve through it with no other packaging change. rpmalloc
(`Unlicense OR MIT`) is left out: its `LICENSE` would collide with
cxxopts' once setuptools < 77 flattens licence files into dist-info,
and the Unlicense option carries no notice requirement.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against mxmlnkn/librapidarchive]
---
 librapidarchive/python/rapidgzip/pyproject.toml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/librapidarchive/python/rapidgzip/pyproject.toml b/librapidarchive/python/rapidgzip/pyproject.toml
index cf09c34..62be663 100644
--- a/librapidarchive/python/rapidgzip/pyproject.toml
+++ b/librapidarchive/python/rapidgzip/pyproject.toml
@@ -75,4 +75,6 @@ py-modules = ["rapidgzip"]
 license-files = [
     "LICENSE-APACHE",
     "LICENSE-MIT",
+    "src/external/cxxopts/LICENSE",
+    "src/external/zlib-ng/LICENSE.md",
 ]
